    "headline_text": "Capital Chronicle report update: Source: U.S. Energy Information Administration, 15 October 2026; week ending 9 October. Commercial crude inventories fell 8.6 million barrels to 415.6 million, while imports fell 791,000 barrels per day. Gasoline stocks rose 3.5 million barrels; distillate stocks fell 2.5 million. These are original EIA balance data retained on 18 October, not a release-time surprise estimate.",
