          "producer_layer": "OBSERVED_SOURCE_FACT",
          "text": "Source: U.S. Energy Information Administration, 15 October 2026; week ending 9 October. Commercial crude inventories fell 8.6 million barrels to 415.6 million, while imports fell 791,000 barrels per day. Gasoline stocks rose 3.5 million barrels; distillate stocks fell 2.5 million. These are original EIA balance data retained on 18 October, not a release-time surprise estimate."
        },
        {
          "basis_risk": "US physical-balance context is not the price or execution economics of the USOIL CFD.",
          "claim_id": "oil-balance-mechanism",
          "producer_layer": "CC_ANALYSIS",
          "text": "Capital Chronicle analysis: the crude and distillate draws support a qualified supply-buffer watch. Lower imports, a gasoline build and softer four-week gasoline demand oppose a simple broad-demand-boom interpretation. Persistence needs further releases; current market pricing is unobserved."
        },
        {
          "basis_risk": "US physical-balance context is not the price or execution economics of the USOIL CFD.",
